cff-version: 1.1.0
message: "If you use SCON, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "SCON: School Counselling Ontology Network"
abstract: >-
  SCON is a modular, BFO-grounded OWL 2 DL ontology for comprehensive counselling across
  the academic, career, and social-emotional domains in school and higher-education
  settings. It comprises 472 classes, 56 object properties and 36 data properties across
  9 modules, with a textual definition on every primitive class, six defined classes
  placed by the reasoner, and 36 competency questions embedded as machine-readable
  annotations. It is released with a synthetic validation dataset of 1,000 de-identified
  students and an executable SPARQL suite.
type: software
